# oracle: compute ave/sphere/atom cutoff 1.6 on a fluid of 108 lj atoms (fcc 0.8442, velocity create 1.2), 20 steps of nve; the density and temperature of the sphere around each atom are dumped at step 20 and summed in thermo
# oracle: native: b332f28 (installed lmp; compute ave/sphere/atom is in the EXTRA-COMPUTE package of that binary)
# oracle-files: w227xc_ave_sphere.dump
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=none filerel=1e-12
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native (thermo rows, final atoms): thermo 3.8e-15, atoms n/a (atoms=none; the per-atom density and temperature are the dump file, worst token 3e-15).
units           lj
atom_style      atomic
lattice         fcc 0.8442
region          box block 0 3 0 3 0 3
create_box      1 box
create_atoms    1 box
mass            1 1.0
velocity        all create 1.2 87287 loop geom
pair_style      lj/cut 2.5
pair_coeff      1 1 1.0 1.0 2.5
compute         av all ave/sphere/atom cutoff 1.6
compute         avS all reduce sum c_av[1] c_av[2]
dump            d1 all custom 20 w227xc_ave_sphere.dump id c_av[1] c_av[2]
dump_modify     d1 sort id format float %.15g
fix             1 all nve
thermo_style    custom step pe ke c_avS[1] c_avS[2]
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          10
run             20
